            <ArticleTitle>Pain in the ear resulting from misplaced subclavian dialysis catheter into ipsilateral internal jugular vein.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1460-1, table of contents</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="IMPLICATIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">This case describes pain in the ear resulting from inadvertent placement of a subclavian dialysis catheter into the ipsilateral internal jugular vein. The pain subsided when the catheter was withdrawn.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
